#: ../../content/C3_rsgp_houses_simulation.rst:64
msgid ""
"The device modeling framework organizes electrical devices into "
"categories. Each category implements specialized ADSR parameters and wave"
" modulation to capture the unique behavior of the device."
msgstr ""
"ينظم إطار عمل نمذجة الأجهزة الأجهزة الكهربائية في فئات. تطبق كل فئة "
"معايير ADSR متخصصة وتعديل الموجة لالتقاط السلوك الفريد للجهاز."

#: ../../content/C3_rsgp_houses_simulation.rst:67
msgid "Integration with Power Management"
msgstr "التكامل مع إدارة الطاقة"

#: ../../content/C3_rsgp_houses_simulation.rst:68
msgid ""
"The ``HousesSimulator`` provides the aggregated system load to the "
"``PowerManager``, along the specific load for each house in the "
"simulation. The ``PowerManager`` then does its calculation and may "
"communicate back to the simulation, connecting or disconnecting some of "
"the houses' load or utility lines. The ``HouseSimulator`` thus offers an "
"interface for the ``PowerManager`` to read the data it needs and modify "
"the simulation per its judgment."
msgstr ""
"يقدم ``محاكي المنازل`` الحمل المجمع للنظام إلى ``مدير الطاقة``، مع الحمل "
"المحدد لكل منزل في المحاكاة. يقوم ``مدير الطاقة`` بعد ذلك بحساباته ويمكن "
"أن يتواصل مع المحاكاة، يربط أو يفصل بعض خطوط حمل المنازل أو خطوط المرافق."
" بهذا يقدم ``محاكي المنزل`` واجهة ل``مدير الطاقة`` لقراءة البيانات التي "
"يحتاجها وتعديل المحاكاة حسب رأيه."

#: ../../content/C3_rsgp_houses_simulation.rst:70
msgid ""
"The interface maintains loose coupling between the ``HouseSimulator`` and"
" the ``PowerManager`` to enable independent development and testing."
msgstr ""
"تحافظ الواجهة على الاقتران الرخو بين ``محاكي المنزل`` و``مدير الطاقة`` "
"لتمكين التطوير والاختبار المستقل."

#: ../../content/C3_rsgp_houses_simulation.rst:73
msgid "Data Collection and Analysis"
msgstr "جمع وتحليل البيانات"

#: ../../content/C3_rsgp_houses_simulation.rst:74
msgid ""
"The houses simulation captures device operation statistics and system "
"performance metrics for later analysis. The data is stored as a time-"
"series dataset (in a CSV file) to enable examination of the effectiveness"
" of power management solutions."
msgstr ""
"تلتقط محاكاة المنازل إحصائيات تشغيل الأجهزة ومقاييس أداء النظام للتحليل "
"اللاحق. يتم تخزين البيانات كمجموعة بيانات زمنية (في ملف CSV) لتمكين فحص "
"فعالية حلول إدارة الطاقة."

#: ../../content/C3_rsgp_houses_simulation.rst:76
msgid ""
"CSV logging operates in the update cycle (usually once every "
"100-milliseconds). It records total house loads, individual device loads,"
" connectivity states, and utility exchange values for each house "
"throughout the simulation. The goal is to track the utility exchange "
"power and minimize it through an effective power management solution."
msgstr ""
"يعمل تسجيل CSV في دورة التحديث (عادة مرة كل 100 ملي ثانية). يسجل إجمالي "
"أحمال المنزل، وأحمال الأجهزة الفردية، وحالات الاتصال، وقيم تبادل المرافق "
"لكل منزل عبر المحاكاة. الهدف هو تتبع طاقة تبادل المرافق وتقليلها من خلال "
"حل فعال لإدارة الطاقة."

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:2
msgid "RSGP Solar System Simulation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:5
msgid ""
"The solar system simulation serves as the source of power within the "
"system. This chapter examines the implementation of photovoltaic panel "
"modeling, battery energy storage systems, and inverter control mechanisms"
" that enable realistic solar power generation and management."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:7
msgid ""
"While the houses simulation models energy consumption, the solar system "
"simulation models energy production and storage. Together they form the "
"fundamental supply-demand dynamic that defines smart grids. The power "
"management system, discussed in later chapters, coordinates between these"
" two to optimize energy usage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:10
msgid "Solar System Architecture Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:11
msgid ""
"The solar system simulation architecture consists of photovoltaic panels,"
" one battery, and an inverter connecting the elements. The inverter is "
"then connected to the power manager through a load line and a utility "
"line. This design separates concerns between energy generation, storage, "
"and power conversion and enables more realistic modeling of each "
"component."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:38
msgid ""
"The **Panels** handle solar irradiance calculations and power generation "
"based on the data collected from the National Solar Radiation Database "
"(NSRDB). The **Battery** manages charge state tracking. The **Inverter** "
"adheres to its operational mode control and manages power distribution "
"from and to the solar system components and the demands of the power "
"manager."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:40
msgid ""
"The three-component architecture enables independent development and "
"testing of solar generation, energy storage, and power distribution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:43
msgid "Photovoltaic Panel Modeling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:44
msgid ""
"The photovoltaic panels integrate with the National Solar Radiation "
"Database to obtain weather information and employs the PVLib photovoltaic"
" modeling library to perform accurate solar calculations. The panel model"
" accounts for solar position, atmospheric conditions, and system "
"configuration parameters to generate power output that mirror actual "
"photovoltaic system performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:62
msgid ""
"The NSRDB contains hourly solar irradiance measurements, temperature "
"data, and atmospheric conditions for locations across the United States. "
"In the simulation, only data local to Phoenix/Arizona was used. The "
"simulation system processes this data to extract direct normal irradiance"
" (DNI), diffuse horizontal irradiance (DHI), and global horizontal "
"irradiance (GHI) values necessary for photovoltaic calculations. The "
"database integration includes automatic timestamp conversion, timezone "
"handling, and data interpolation to support accelerated simulation time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:64
msgid ""
"Solar position calculations account for latitude, longitude, time of "
"year, and time of day to determine solar azimuth and elevation angles. "
"The solar position information combines with irradiance data (DNI, DHI, "
"and GHI) to calculate the effective solar energy. The PVLib library "
"performs these calculations using established solar position algorithms. "
"Below is an overview of the parameters of that calculation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:66
msgid ""
"**Direct Normal Irradiance (DNI)** represents the irradiance directly "
"from the sun to the surface of the photovoltaic panels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:68
msgid ""
"**Diffuse Horizontal Irradiance(DHI)** represents the irradiance "
"indirectly reaching the surface of the photovoltaic panels through the "
"rays scattered by the sky dome."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:70
msgid ""
"**Global Horizontal Irradiance(GHI)** represents the total irradiance, "
"calculated by the following formula: GHI = DNI * cos(θ) + DHI, where θ is"
" the solar zenith angle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:72
msgid ""
"The simulation supports configurable panel count, individual panel area, "
"and conversion efficiency specifications that determine total array "
"capacity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:75
msgid "Battery Energy Storage System"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:76
msgid ""
"The battery system implement lithium-ion battery characteristics "
"including charge acceptance, storage capacity, and charge efficiency. The"
" model provides an interface to the inverter to charge and discharge from"
" the battery as per its calculations. As such, the battery component "
"itself is devoid of any calculations beside implementing its charge "
"efficiency and limitations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:78
msgid ""
"The battery can alse be configured on the maximum charge current it can "
"accept, and the maximum discharge. This models the safety considerations "
"present in actual batteries as they reject currents above a certain "
"level."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:81
msgid "Inverter Control System"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:82
msgid ""
"The inverter manages power flow between the photovoltaic panels, battery,"
" and the power manager. It implements DC to AC conversion modeling to "
"account for power losses that occur when converting direct current from "
"the photovoltaic panels and the battery to alternating current for load "
"consumption and utility export. The conversion is handled by the PVWatts "
"library that follows established algorithms to accurately model the "
"conversion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:84
msgid "The inverter implements three operating modes for power flow priority."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:86
msgid ""
"**Solar-Battery-Utility (SBU) mode** prioritizes using the power "
"available from the photovoltaic panels if present, and only when the "
"panels by themselves do not meet the load that it draws from the battery."
" When the battery is empty, only then would the inverter draw from "
"utility. This mode aims to reduce grid-dependency to a minimum."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:88
msgid ""
"**Solar-Utility-Battery (SUB) mode** prioritizes using the power "
"available from the photovoltaic panels--just like the previous mode. "
"However, when the panels power prove insufficient, it draws from utility "
"to meet the demand and keeps the battery as only a last resort when no "
"other source of energy exists. This mode aims to provide security and "
"prepare to meet emergencies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:90
msgid ""
"**Utility-Solar-Battery (USB) mode** prioritizes drawing from utility. It"
" uses the solar system as only a back-up in case the utility is out of "
"service."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:92
msgid ""
"The power manager can switch the operation mode of the inverter. This may"
" prove useful in scenarios where the battery should be reserved for a "
"foreseen emergency, thus switching the operation mode to SUB to use the "
"utility now and keep the battery to be used when neither the solar panels"
" nor the utility can provide power. While the capability for this "
"currently exists in the system, the power manager carries out no such "
"switches as it currently lacks the ability to predict emergencies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:94
msgid ""
"Additionally, the inverter implements a charge priority, which determines"
" how excess solar power gets allocated between battery charging and "
"utility export. The system supports multiple charge priority settings "
"including solar-only charging, solar-first charging, and utility-assisted"
" charging modes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:96
msgid ""
"**Solar-only** directs all excess solar power to battery charging before "
"any utility export occurs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:98
msgid ""
"**Solar-first** uses the excess solar power to charge the battery when "
"present. When not present, it uses the utility to charge the battery."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:100
msgid ""
"**Utility-assisted** enables battery charging from utility power even "
"when some excess solar power is present."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:102
msgid ""
"In all charge priorities, the inverter will export to utility only when "
"the battery is full."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:104
msgid ""
"The inverter implements load shedding as a protective measure that "
"prevents system overload. It disconnects the load when available power "
"sources prove insufficient. The load is then automatically reconnected "
"after a set period of time, during which the power manager should have "
"taken care of the issue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:106
msgid ""
"The power manager ensures that load shedding may not happen as it "
"automatically disconnects loads from the specific houses that are "
"overusing. As such, load shedding is only ever triggered in the extreme "
"situations where the power manager fails."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:109
msgid "Weather Data Integration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:110
msgid ""
"This component manages the interface between the simulation environment "
"and the external weather database, ensuring that solar calculations "
"reflect actual atmospheric conditions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:112
msgid ""
"The National Solar Radiation Database is the primary data source for "
"solar irradiance and atmospheric conditions. The NSRDB provides hourly "
"measurements of solar radiation components (DNI, DHI, and GHI), ambient "
"temperature, wind speed, and other meteorological parameters collected at"
" numerous locations across the United States. This database is one of the"
" most comprehensive sources of solar data available for renewable energy "
"applications, providing the data necessary for detailed photovoltaic "
"system modeling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:114
msgid ""
"The database used from NSRDB covers the aforementioned measurements taken"
" in the Phoenix/Arizona for one full year; one record each half an hour. "
"Data is extracted using the simulation time; the record with the "
"timestamp closest to the current simulation timestamp is used for the "
"calculations of the solar energy in that specific moment in the "
"simulation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:117
msgid "Power Management Interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:118
msgid ""
"The solar system takes in the load from the power manager and gives back "
"the solar panel power used, battery discharged, and grid import or "
"export. The power manager then uses these data to take decisions "
"regarding the load. The interface is two-way; the power manager provides "
"the load, and the solar system provides metrics specifying how the load "
"is being met."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:120
msgid ""
"Currently, the interface consists purely of the exchange of data; there "
"is no exchange of commands or requests between the components."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:123
#, fuzzy
msgid "Data Collection"
msgstr "جمع وتحليل البيانات"

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:124
msgid ""
"Data collection operates continuously throughout simulation to capture "
"time-series data about solar generation, battery operation, and system-"
"wide energy flows. The collected data can then be analyzed to pinpoint "
"issues in the model and help refine both the simulation and the power "
"management solutions. Utility import and export represent the most "
"important metrics collected, as they are direct metrics of the "
"effectiveness of the power management solution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:126
msgid ""
"The system captures data from all the components to enable any form of "
"analysis. The data collection is extensive: state-of-charge of the "
"battery, power generated from the panels, the system-wide load, utility "
"import and export, among other metrics. The data is logged to a CSV file "
"continuously throughout the simulation. Along the data from NSRDB, the "
"logged CSV files provide all the data needed to carry out analysis on the"
" trends of power generation and consumption. Trend analysis might lead to"
" improvements on the power management solutions. Additionally, AI "
"techniques can be used to benefit from the data and extend the power "
"manager with AI capabilities. This could be especially useful to predict "
"shortages of power generation and thus switch the operation mode of the "
"inverter to import from utility to keep the battery for that shortage and"
" thus maintain long-term system stability."
msgstr ""

